WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:05.332
Find the demo yarns in Rate Book, and check
which saved quality uses them.

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:15.256
Update the weft rate to one hundred and forty
rupees per kilogram.

3
00:00:15.496 --> 00:00:18.845
Add a supplier note so you can identify the
source.

4
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:30.437
Save the new rate, then open Activity to review
the recorded change and its history.

5
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.159
Reopen the linked saved quality.

6
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.424
The weft rate now includes your update.

7
00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:52.837
Apply the quality and check its yarn inputs.

8
00:00:53.077 --> 00:00:58.099
Open Live Cost to review the recalculated
production cost and selling price.

9
00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:10.983
Now open an earlier saved costing to compare it
with the updated estimate.

10
00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.668
The earlier costing keeps its original figures.

11
00:01:16.908 --> 00:01:20.790
Changing Rate Book does not rewrite saved
costing snapshots.
